  "verdict": "PARTIAL. The structural leakage claim is VERIFIED and large: the row-level split places 6,833 patients in both train and test, and ~42% of test rows belong to a patient seen in training. A sensitive within-split difference-in-differences does detect a genuine leakage advantage on the leaked stratum (+0.025 AUROC, 95% CI excludes 0). However the implied consequence for the PUBLISHED headline number is NOT supported: switching to GroupShuffleSplit changes pooled test AUROC by -0.0022 (95% CI [-0.0058, +0.0014]) over 20 seeds, i.e. indistinguishable from zero and smaller than split-to-split noise. The reported AUROC ~0.64 is not materially inflated by the leakage."
